  "limitations": [
    "Exact image C is the behavior authority; native C is an auxiliary signal control.",
    "F02 daemon reproductions cover ordinary and debug TCP and UDP cached-CNAME TXT controls, plus fresh retained NXDOMAIN followed by actual DHCP publication. They do not exhaust every CNAME/RR/RD/DO/stale combination.",
    "The published-DHCP probe intentionally uses --fresh-only; the previously excluded stale EDE difference is not claimed fixed.",
    "F06 daemon probe exercises an existing lo scope and an IPv4 control with zero upstream traffic; other scope forms and counter workloads require their separate regression evidence.",
    "Only these four selected commands are closed here; the complete affected-family outcome is recorded separately.",
    "Hashes bind scripts, retained result bytes and supplied ELF files; these probes do not independently attest /proc/PID/exe for every process."
  ]
}
